A prefix ++/-- targets the LAST step of the chain, not the first.

WHAT IT IS. `--p->n` computed `&p + offset` -- the member offset added to the
address of the LOCAL VARIABLE p -- and decremented whatever stack slot that
landed on.

    sub_x0,x13,8        # &p
    mov_x14,8           # -> offset calculation
    add_x0,x14,x0       # &p + 8       <-- a stack slot, not a member
    ldr_x0,[x0]

`primary_expr` carries a flag, prefix_lvalue, meaning "do not load this
variable, the caller wants its address". That is right when the variable IS the
target -- `--n` -- and wrong the moment anything stands between it and the
target, because then the address wanted is p's VALUE plus the offset. The flag
was applied to the first node of the chain instead of the last.

`p->n++` was always right, and the reason is the whole shape of this class: a
POSTFIX operator sits where a lookahead can see it, so postfix_expr_arrow tests
the token in front of it and suppresses its own load. A PREFIX operator was
consumed before the chain was parsed and no lookahead there can see it. Ninth
instance of one-rule-several-implementations in this series, and the second
where a global flag was right for the simple case and wrong across a chain --
Address_of was the first.

HOW IT WAS FOUND, BECAUSE THE ROUTE MATTERS MORE THAN THE FIX.

The symptom was three frames away. tcc reported

    <command line>:27: warning: extra tokens after directive

on the first `#if` of its own predefs. skip_to_eol was told the token was not a
linefeed. It was:

    LEFTOVER tok=655360        TOK_LINEFEED is 10.  655360 is 10 << 16.

Not a shift -- a base pointer. Probing expr_preprocess across the end_macro()
call gave every local shifted identically:

    before  t=10       t0=256       str=23066160        &t=...567320
    after   t=655360   t0=16777216  str=1511663861760   &t=...567318

which is what reading eight bytes from an address TWO BYTES LOW looks like. The
stack pointer measured identical either side, so only the saved locals pointer
came back wrong.

Four reductions by SHAPE all passed -- an identical static copy of end_macro
reproduced it, and the same statements split across two calls did not, so it
was not the construct. Snapshotting 96 words of the frame across the call named
the exact slot and the exact delta:

    SLOT -6   old=70368752567336   new=70368752567334   delta=-2

A poor-man's watchpoint on that address, armed from a global so it survived the
corrupted frame, caught the writer:

    W2 after free_str delta=-1

tok_str_free -> tal_free_impl, whose second statement is

    if (0 == --al->nb_allocs)                        tccpp.c

That is the construct. It runs on every token string tcc frees, and in that
frame the stray decrement landed on the caller's saved locals pointer.

    guessing at the shape:    5 attempts, 0 hits
    following the write:      1 attempt, exact

THE FIX. When a `->` follows the variable, prefix_lvalue no longer suppresses
its load -- the pointer is needed -- and prefix_lvalue_target carries the "you
are the lvalue" instruction to the arrow site, which suppresses ITS final load
instead. The flag is set and cleared inside one statement, and cleared again in
the prefix handler if the chain never reached an arrow, because a global that
outlives its statement is exactly how Address_of earned its section in
MICRO-C.md.

Only the pointer form is redirected. `--s.n` needs no load -- `&s + offset` IS
the member -- and `--a[i]` has cases behind it. Neither is touched.

WHAT IT DOES NOT DO, AND A SECOND BUG FOUND ON THE WAY.

`--s.n` on a LOCAL STRUCT is also wrong. It was found while writing case 55 and
is NOT fixed here: it is a different site with a different cause, and the first
attempt at a joint fix -- suppressing the dot site's final load under the same
flag -- did not close it. That is evidence, not an assumption, and it is why
the two are separate. It is case 57, marked KNOWN GAP, so it cannot be
forgotten and cannot quietly go green without being noticed.

MEASURED

    difftest         55 pass / 0 fail / 2 known gaps, BOTH architectures
    vocabulary       clean on five architectures
    imm-identity     104 byte-identical, 4 declared, 0 undeclared
    tcc              "extra tokens after directive" is GONE -- tcc now
                     preprocesses its own predefs with no diagnostic at all
    fault            still SIGSEGV, and the marker trail has not been re-read
                     since; that is the next round's measurement, not a claim
                     made here

